## Dataset Characteristics & Variable Dictionary (N = 303)

The final analytical sample (N = 303) reflects verified responses collected between 10 March and 15 April 2026:
- **Demographics:** Female (Gender = 1): 215 (70.96%), Male (Gender = 0): 88 (29.04%).
- **Professional Categories:** Undergraduate Students (n = 224, 73.93%), Academic/Graduate Researchers (n = 54, 17.82%), Licensed Practicing Pharmacists (n = 25, 8.25%).
- **Experience Levels:** <1 year (26.40%), 1–5 years (50.50%), 6–10 years (14.85%), >10 years (8.25%).

### Core Construct Specifications (Formative Composite Indices, 0–100 Scale)
- `PILS_pct`: Pharmaceutical IP Literacy Score (9 objective binary legal items, Mean = 38.87 +/- 15.55%, Median = 44.44%).
- `IAI_pct`: Intellectual Property Attitude Index (10 Likert items, Mean = 71.30 +/- 8.27%, Median = 72.50%).
- `IRS_pct`: Perceived Institutional Readiness Score (4 Likert items on TTOs, funding, legal support; Mean = 17.82 +/- 20.35%, 48.51% zeros).
- `IPI_pct`: Innovation Practice Index (3 behavioral items on patents, R&D, tech transfer; Mean = 10.45 +/- 17.91%, 71.95% zeros).
- `Diagnostic_Gap`: Arithmetic difference (IAI_pct - IPI_pct, Mean = 60.84 +/- 19.93 points).

---

## Instructions for Reproduction

To reproduce all tables, statistics, and regression models in the manuscript:

1. Install required dependencies:
   `pip install -r requirements.txt`

2. Execute the reproducible statistical analysis codebase:
   `python reproducible_statistical_analysis.py`

---

## Ethical Compliance & Citation

- **IRB Ethical Approval:** Formal approval granted by the Institutional Review Board (IRB) of Manara University, Syria (Approval No. `MU-URO-26-02`).
- **Data Archiving:** Permanently archived on Zenodo (DOI: 10.5281/zenodo.20716882).
- **Citation:**
  > Khatib, C., Alkozy, H., Hamdan, Z., Isber, M., & Mlhem, J. (2026). *Pharmaceutical Innovation in Syria: Readiness and Practice Gaps*. Eastern Mediterranean Health Journal (EMHJ / WHO EMRO). Dataset & Code Repository.
    
